// EXPECT: [E012]
// EXPECT-TEXT: Error Ln 7, Col 12: `~` complements an integer, and its operand is 'f64'.
// I.154: `~` on a float was typed i32 and went on to C, `v2 = ~v0` on a double, which gcc refuses
// ("wrong type argument to bit-complement"). So did `~` on an f32x4. Spec 08: the bitwise
// operators take integers.
func f(y f64) f64 {
    return ~y
}

func main() i32 { return 0 }
